      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The baseline coating has a standard microstructure and grain size optimized for room-temperature applications.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlled pre-annealing can refine the coating's grain-boundary structure and create engineered nanostructured grain boundaries.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Engineered nanostructured grain boundaries act as rapid diffusion paths during thermal exposure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enhanced diffusion in a thin film can accelerate elemental segregation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6416794::web::014::3_results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Thermal exposure allows coating elements to react with oxygen and form surface oxides.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10908794::web::037::microstructure_investigation"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pre-annealing accelerates segregation of reactive elements to the FeNiCrCoCu coating surface.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pre-annealing promotes rapid formation of a continuous, adherent oxide or tribochemical film.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10908794::web::037::microstructure_investigation"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting oxide or tribochemical film is self-lubricating.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A protective oxide layer can enhance coating wear resistance after high-temperature exposure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10908794::web::037::microstructure_investigation"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The protective surface film reduces both abrasive and adhesive wear relative to an untreated coating.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pre-annealed FeNiCrCoCu coatings will form protective oxide or tribofilms faster and more robustly than as-deposited coatings.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pre-annealed coatings will have lower wear rates than as-deposited coatings.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pre-annealed coatings will have lower coefficients of friction than as-deposited coatings.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed mechanism applies over 600–800 °C.",
